# CashClip — App Signing & Version State

> **Template** — copy this file to `SIGNING.md` in the same directory and fill
> in the values for your local signing credentials.  `SIGNING.md` is
> gitignored (it contains sensitive credential paths); this template is
> tracked so the format stays consistent across contributors.

---

## Pre-push version-sync hook

A pre-push hook (`scripts/git-hooks/pre-push`, tracked in the repository)
automatically runs `pnpm --filter @workspace/scripts run check-signing-md-sync`
whenever a push contains commits that touch `artifacts/cashclip/app.json` or
`artifacts/cashclip/SIGNING.md`.

**Setting up the hook** — after cloning or when first enabling this feature,
run `pnpm install` from the workspace root (or the `prepare` script
explicitly).  This registers `scripts/git-hooks/` as the active hooks
directory for your local clone:

```sh
pnpm install          # runs `git config core.hooksPath scripts/git-hooks`
# or explicitly:
git config core.hooksPath scripts/git-hooks
```

**Opting in to the check** — the hook exits 0 immediately when `SIGNING.md`
is absent, so contributors who have not created it are unaffected.  The check
only runs actively once you create your local `SIGNING.md` from this template.

**Skipping once** — if you need to push without running the check (e.g. during
a merge-conflict resolution), use:

```sh
git push --no-verify
```

**Running the check manually** at any time:

```sh
pnpm --filter @workspace/scripts run check-signing-md-sync
# or from the workspace root:
pnpm run check-signing-md-sync
```

**Keeping SIGNING.md in sync** — always use the bump scripts rather than
editing `app.json` directly:

```sh
# Bump build number only (most common):
pnpm --filter @workspace/scripts run bump-build-number

# Bump semver version AND build number:
pnpm --filter @workspace/scripts run bump-version -- patch   # or minor / major
```

